finding: src/standard/rendering/cluster.ts:877 sets lightGridPopulated=false when the empty-light transition clear is only encoded, not submitted. If a later draw system propagates an error, World.abortDrawGroup (src/engine/ecs/world.ts:235-255) discards that clear while the flag remains false. The next healthy zero-light frame skips clearing at cluster.ts:868, so shading reads the old nonempty grid and old light/index data indefinitely (engine.ts:120-125). Independently reproduced on this HEAD with a camera and PointLight: first frame had 2074 nonempty clusters; remove PointLight, throw from a draw system ordered after CullLightsSystem, catch step's error, disable the throw and step again: still 2074 nonempty clusters. The existing empty/lit/empty check passes because all its encoded clears are submitted. This fails the stage's stale-grid safety claim; the transition's CPU flag must not outrun successful submission or must be invalidated after an aborted frame.
